{
  "$Comment": "Ice King's staff poses: vanilla Skeleton_Staff (Parent) with CastSummon (the ice ray cast) swapped for editable copies of the vanilla Staff Cast_Summon. The Moving copy keys only the upper body, so the legs and beard keep the Fly animation while he casts in the air. SwingLeft (scepter) is a copy of the vanilla Spear entry with the king's own ThirdPersonFace: the vanilla faces (Frown, Rage) move the node 'Mouth' to empty cells of the king's mouth sheet and his mouth vanished. Face_Clench = clenched teeth, Face_Shout = big shout. Per-attack entries (2026-10-21, wanted: each attack editable on its own, with English names): SummonGuntersCharging/SummonGuntersCast (summon), IceNovaCharging/IceNovaBlast (nova), IcebergCharging/IcebergCast (iceberg), each with its own copy of the Staff cast files (Summon_Gunters_*, Ice_Nova_*, Iceberg_*); same settings as CastSummonCharging/Charged. The interactions use these ItemAnimationIds; the shared CastSummonCharging/Charged overrides were removed once nothing used them (they fall back to Skeleton_Staff's). More per-attack entries (2026-10-21, mechanics pass's new attacks): ZapCast (Zap, copy of CastSummon), IceShieldHold/IceShieldBurst (Defens-ice), IceRainCharging/IceRainCast (ice rain), both copies of the iceberg pair, FrostBeamCharging/FrostBeamFire (charged beam, copies of the nova pair); charging = Face_Clench, release = Face_Shout. Starting files are exact copies to animate by hand. Ultimate (2026-10-21): FrostUltimateCharging (1 s loop: the charge orb grows and spins at his chest), FrostUltimateFire (2.8 s: the Frost_Beam attachment shoots out 24 blocks forward, flickers and spins, then thins out), FrostUltimateRecovery (1.2 s back to rest, the orb fades); body poses from the FrostBeam pair. Ultimate faces (2026-10-21): keyed inside Frost_Ultimate_Charging (mouth closed, brows half frowned) and Frost_Ultimate_Fire (big shout + angry brows from 0.1 s), so those two entries have no ThirdPersonFace. Ice burst bolts (2026-10-21): FrostBeamFire = his right-hand throw (Frost_Beam_Fire, 0.5 s) and FrostBeamFireL = its mirror with the left hand (Frost_Beam_Fire_L), both at Speed 2 (0.25 s per bolt) with the big shout and angry brows keyed inside, so no ThirdPersonFace; the burst alternates them, one per bolt. FrostBeamFireBoth (2026-10-21: aerial burst variant): both arms thrust forward together from the hands-by-the-head charge, one throw = two bolts (one per hand); Speed 2, shout + angry brows inside. Nova (2026-10-21): charging = half crouch covering himself (arms crossed, chest bent), blast = stands up and throws the arms wide; burst charging = hands raised beside the head (concept art). IceRayThrow / IceRayThrowL (2026-10-21: the single ice ray should also throw with one hand, sometimes right, sometimes left): the same right/left throw files as the burst, at normal speed (0.5 s). CastSummon removed 2026-10-21: the rays now use IceRayThrow/IceRayThrowL and nothing else played it (falls back to Skeleton_Staff's if ever asked for); its Cast_Summon files went to backups. FrostBeamChargingBoth (2026-10-21): the hands-beside-the-head charge, only before the two-hand throws (FrostBeamFireBoth); FrostBeamCharging is again his one-hand wind-up (right arm back), for the one-hand burst and the ice ray. FrostBeamChargingL (2026-10-21): mirror of his one-hand wind-up with the LEFT arm drawn back, to go before IceRayThrowL / FrostBeamFireL. IceRayThrow/IceRayThrowL now have their own files (Ice_Ray_Throw, Ice_Ray_Throw_L): the throwing hand ends in front of the face centre (the ray bolt leaves at X 0); the burst throws end at X ±0.2 like their bolts. IceSwordSwing1 / IceSwordSwing2 (2026-10-21, mechanics: an air sword combo summon -> swing 1 -> swing 2 -> IceSwordSlash): 0.45 s each, Ice_Sword_Held shown the whole time and the staff tucked away (R-Attachment z -36); swing 1 = forehand from his right to his left, slightly downward, swing 2 = backhand from his left to his right that ends with the sword back overhead, where the chop starts; the blade crosses his front at 0.167 s (frame 10), when the hit lands. Each swing starts where the one before ends (summon end -> swing 1 -> swing 2 -> chop start). Swing 1 = Face_Clench, swing 2 = Face_Shout. Ice mace (2026-10-21: instead of the drum solo, he takes an ice mace and slams the ground making waves to jump over): IceMaceSummon (0.6 s, holds) = the mace grows in his raised right hand, then both hands take it cocked behind his head; IceMaceSlam (0.67 s, holds) = two-hand slam over his head into the ground in front of him, impact at 0.2 s (frame 12), crouch on the recoil and back to the cocked pose at the end, so it can be played again for more waves; IceMaceSlamLast (0.87 s, holds) = the same slam, then the mace swells and bursts away (0.4-0.47 s) and he straightens up. The mace head lands about 1.2 blocks in front of him, a quarter block to his right. PunchR / PunchL (2026-10-21: MeleeHit's hit came long after the punch, and it should alternate fists): right / left straight punch, 0.6 s, fist fully out at 0.2 s (frame 12) and held to 0.28 s, the other fist guarding the chin, the held weapon tucked (R-Attachment z -36); for an interaction with a 0.2 s prepare RunTime. Upper body only, so the same file works moving. ZapCastL (2026-10-21: the zap should alternate hands): ZapCast's throw mirrored to the LEFT hand (Zap_Throw_L / _Moving, same 42 frames, arm out at frame 15), staff tuck kept on R-Attachment.",
